  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The distance between charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi></math> and between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>l</mi></math>. The electrostatic potential at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> from centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>α</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, where the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math> is ______. (Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><img src=\"assets\\qt0053_2561eed633d8.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 186px;\"/>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "27",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Considering two dipoles with charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi><mo> </mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo> </mo><mi>q</mi></math>, we can write the equivalent setup as shown below:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0053_7ced6008e33e.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 150px;\"/></p><p>Therefore, net dipole moment is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></math> in the leftward direction.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0053_142ccebc716f.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 199px;\"/></p><p>Potential required, </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>·</mo><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><msup><mn>120</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mfenced><mn>27</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup></math></p><p>Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}